    {
      "id": "sticky-overview",
      "name": "Note: Workflow Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-200, 0],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## WF-S02: Self-Healing Incident Response\n\n**Triggers:**\n- Webhook: `/webhook/alert`\n- Schedule: Every 2 minutes\n\n**Purpose:** Detect and auto-remediate system issues\n\n### Severity Levels:\n- P1: Critical (crash, DB down, broker disconnect)\n- P2: High (unresponsive agent, high memory)\n- P3: Medium (stale heartbeat, high CPU)\n- P4: Low (informational)\n\n### Auto-Fix Strategies:\n- restart_agent: POST /api/control {restart}\n- restart_service: Docker restart\n- clear_cache: Cache invalidation\n- reconnect_broker: Broker reconnection\n\n### Retry Logic:\n- P1: 3 retries, 30s delay\n- P2: 2 retries, 45s delay\n- P3: 1 retry, 60s delay"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-escalation",
      "name": "Note: Escalation Path",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [4540, 0],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Escalation Path\n\n1. Auto-fix attempted\n2. If fails: Wait + Retry (up to maxRetries)\n3. If still fails: Mark for escalation\n4. Post to #chief Discord\n5. Create PULSE Jira ticket\n6. If P1/P2: Trigger post-mortem workflow\n\n### Post-Mortem (P1/P2 only):\n- Creates detailed incident timeline\n- Schedules review meeting\n- Generates lessons learned ticket"
      }
    }
